# Learning Loop & Promotion Levels

Spec: LearningLoop
Purpose:
  Define the full learning loop pipeline that drives AI knowledge
  evolution from raw observation to project rule, and the L0-L4
  promotion levels that gate knowledge advancement. This is the
  conceptual engine; the execution-level endpoint is
  workflow/learning-gate.sdd.

Owns: lifecycle/learning-loop.sdd

## Learning Loop Pipeline

  OBSERVATION
    ↓
  DISCOVERY
    ↓
  CANDIDATE
    ↓
  EVIDENCE
    ↓
  CLAIM
    ↓
  VALIDATION
    ↓
  KNOWLEDGE

  OBSERVATION:
    entity: @observation.*
    description: AI raw observation — a pattern, smell, gap, or drift detected
                 during task execution or code analysis
    trust: low, confidence: low
    example: "DB transaction + event publishing causes inconsistency in 3 projects"

  DISCOVERY:
    entity: @discovery.*
    description: A repeated or strategically important pattern observed across
                 multiple contexts
    trigger: 3+ independent observations of the same pattern, OR 1 strategic
             observation (security-sensitive)
    trust: low, confidence: low | medium

  CANDIDATE:
    entity: @candidate.*
    description: Reusable knowledge candidate that may become a validated skill
    trigger: discovery promoted with evidence
    trust: low (default — no validation yet)
    confidence: low | medium
    TTL: 30 days (expires if not promoted)

  EVIDENCE:
    entity: @evidence.* (or inline evidence on claim)
    description: Collected proof — code references, test results, task outcomes,
                 decision citations, production data
    trust: derived from source (see governance/security-events.sdd)
    confidence: varies by source quality

  CLAIM:
    entity: @claim.*
    description: A single assertable statement backed by evidence
    trust: varies
    confidence: LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH
    lifecycle: PROPOSED → SUPPORTED → VALIDATED → ACTIVE → CHALLENGED → INVALIDATED/SUPERSEDED

  VALIDATION:
    description: Evidence is checked — tests passed, human reviewed,
                 production confirmed
    trigger: promotion gate
    approval: human or automated gate

  KNOWLEDGE:
    entity: @skill.* / @concept.* / @policy.* / @decision.*
    description: Validated, reusable knowledge in the project or organization
    trust: medium | high (never AI-inferred alone)
    confidence: MEDIUM | HIGH

## Knowledge Promotion Levels (L0-L4)

  L0 — Observation (@observation.*)
    description: Seen once in a single context
    example: "Payment retry pattern observed in payment-service"
    promotion_to: L1 requires pattern repetition or strategic relevance
    rule: [PROMO-01] L0 → L1 requires 3+ independent observations OR
          1 strategic observation (security-sensitive).

  L1 — Discovery (@discovery.*)
    description: Repeated pattern, potentially reusable
    example: "Payment retry pattern observed across 5 projects"
    promotion_to: L2 requires evidence gathering
    rule: [PROMO-02] L1 → L2 requires evidence_count >= 2 from
          independent sources with at least one test or human review.

  L2 — Candidate (@candidate.*)
    description: Reusable knowledge that may become a skill
    example: @candidate.payment-retry
    promotion_to: L3 requires validation
    rule: [PROMO-03] L2 → L3 requires VALIDATED claim approval by human.
    rule: [PROMO-04] Candidates expire 30 days without promotion.

  L3 — Validated Knowledge (@skill.*, @concept.*)
    description: Confirmed by tests, tasks, or human review
    example: @skill.idempotent-command
    promotion_to: L4 requires multi-project success evidence
    rule: [PROMO-05] L3 → L4 requires evidence from 2+ distinct projects
          without regression and human approval.

  L4 — Project Rule (@policy.*, @decision.*, @architecture-rule)
    description: Organization-wide or project-wide norm with full authority
    example: @decision.D88 "All payment commands must be idempotent"
    promotion_to: none (highest level)
    rule: [PROMO-06] Only human-approved decisions can reach L4.
    rule: [PROMO-07] L4 knowledge can be challenged but NEVER auto-deprecated.

  Promotion Summary:
    L0 Observation  →  L1 Discovery  →  L2 Candidate  →  L3 Validated Knowledge  →  L4 Project Rule
    (seen once)        (repeated)        (reusable)      (confirmed by evidence)     (norm with authority)

## Bidirectional Knowledge Evolution

  Knowledge is NOT monotonic — promotions can be reversed:

  L4 Project Rule
    ↓ challenge
  L3 Validated Knowledge  (claim invalidated, confidence downgraded)

  L3 Validated Knowledge
    ↓ contradiction
  L2 Candidate            (claim invalidated, sent back for re-validation)

  L2 Candidate
    ↓ evidence invalidated
  L1 Discovery            (new evidence required)

  [BIO-01] Downgrades MUST preserve original evidence and provenance.
  [BIO-02] Downgrades require a @challenge.* or @observation.* justifying the change.
  [BIO-03] The downgrade path is recorded in @generation.* lineage.

## Learning Boundary

  AI capabilities by promotion level:

  CAN DO (without human approval):
    - Observe patterns (L0)
    - Cluster observations into discoveries (L1)
    - Create candidate knowledge (L2)
    - Form claims with evidence (claim layer)
    - Propose promotions (L2 → L3, L3 → L4)

  CANNOT DO (require human approval):
    - Promote L2 → L3 (candidate to validated knowledge)
    - Promote L3 → L4 (validated knowledge to project rule)
    - Invalidate L3 or L4 claims
    - Override a challenge that was accepted by human

  [BOUNDARY-01] AI CAN observe and propose, but CANNOT enforce project rules
                without human approval.
  [BOUNDARY-02] "AI thought" is never "project truth" — validation is the gate.
  [BOUNDARY-03] The learning gate (workflow/learning-gate.sdd) is the execution-
                level checkpoint for this pipeline.

## Integration with Learning Gate

  The learning gate (workflow/learning-gate.sdd) is the per-task execution
  checkpoint that feeds the learning loop:

    Learning Gate Outcomes → Learning Loop Stages
    NO_NEW_KNOWLEDGE       → (loop not triggered)
    EXISTING_KNOWLEDGE_UPDATED → EVIDENCE (link to existing claim)
    NEW_CANDIDATE          → CANDIDATE (L2)
    NEW_VALIDATED_SKILL    → KNOWLEDGE (L3, with human approval)
    NEW_DECISION           → KNOWLEDGE (L4, with human approval)
    NEW_LESSON             → EVIDENCE (negative knowledge)

  [INTEGRATE-01] Learning gate outcomes are mapped to learning loop stages
                 during consolidation at task end.
  [INTEGRATE-02] NEW_VALIDATED_SKILL from learning gate requires human
                 approval to reach L3 — AI proposes only.

